<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Holaspis22 cuticle Turing wavelength at 15 µm (Wenlock, 428.1 Ma) (Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis22 (22 thoracic segments))",
        "Holaspis22 cuticle Turing wavelength at 15 µm (Wenlock, 428.1 Ma) faithfully reproduces Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis22 (22 thoracic segments) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis22 (22 thoracic segments) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis22 (22 thoracic segments)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 18- and 22-segment animals are successive chronospecies separated by 0.2 Myr.",
        "does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg kinetics were written down by Fusco, Hughes, or Turing; Turing 1952 supplies the dispersion relation, Schnakenberg supplies a two-species carrier that realizes it.",
        "does_not_claim: That the fossil photograph resolves 15 µm ocelli.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Entry-size ratio 1.115^4 and the per-tergite wavelength-count ratio against the 18-segment predecessor.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian and k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), with the length unit set so lambda_c = 1.514e-5 m.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Segment-accretion reveal on the pinned dorsal photograph, with the simulated activator painted into the two eye regions.",
        "reported_in_source: A shape transition near glabellar length 1.7 mm is not strictly tied to segment number (Hughes & Chapman 1995).",
        "reported_in_source: Five holaspid morphs with 18–22 thoracic segments; hemianamorphosis; precocious specification of the adult count (Fusco et al. 2004).",
        "reported_in_source: Meraspid per-stage growth 1.115 and holaspid per-stage growth 1.103; thoracic release ends at s18 for t18 and s22 for t22 (Hughes et al. 2017).",
        "transfer_boundary: 15 µm is the assigned cellular detail scale for this slot. It is not a lens diameter measured on Aulacopleura.",
        "transfer_boundary: The catalog ages 428.3 Ma (holaspis18) and 428.1 Ma (holaspis22) are series bookkeeping. Fusco et al. 2004 describe contemporaneous intraspecific morphs from one narrow Wenlock interval near 429 Ma." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Aulacopleura koninckii_holaspis22 (Silurian (Wenlock Epoch, 428.1 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Aulacopleura" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis22 (22 thoracic segments); environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.18.1, pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Five holaspid morphs with 18–22 thoracic segments; hemianamorphosis; precocious specification of the adult count (Fusco et al. 2004). | Meraspid per-stage growth 1.115 and holaspid per-stage growth 1.103; thoracic release ends at s18 for t18 and s22 for t22 (Hughes et al. 2017). | A shape transition near glabellar length 1.7 mm is not strictly tied to segment number (Hughes & Chapman 1995).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian and k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), with the length unit set so lambda_c = 1.514e-5 m. | Entry-size ratio 1.115^4 and the per-tergite wavelength-count ratio against the 18-segment predecessor. | Segment-accretion reveal on the pinned dorsal photograph, with the simulated activator painted into the two eye regions.; transfer_boundary: The catalog ages 428.3 Ma (holaspis18) and 428.1 Ma (holaspis22) are series bookkeeping. Fusco et al. 2004 describe contemporaneous intraspecific morphs from one narrow Wenlock interval near 429 Ma. | 15 µm is the assigned cellular detail scale for this slot. It is not a lens diameter measured on Aulacopleura.; does_not_claim: That the fossil photograph resolves 15 µm ocelli. | That 18- and 22-segment animals are successive chronospecies separated by 0.2 Myr. | That Schnakenberg kinetics were written down by Fusco, Hughes, or Turing; Turing 1952 supplies the dispersion relation, Schnakenberg supplies a two-species carrier that realizes it.]; phenomenon_size: 11 µm (1.088e-05 m, log10=-4.963 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 11 µm to 2.4 cm): 11 µm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-bioelectric-polarity, 34 µm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-vertex-packing, 544 µm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength, 1.1 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-clock-wavefront, 2.4 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-morphogen-condensation, 3.0 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-elastic-buckling, 3.4 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-flux-canalization, 4.8 mm:aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-branching-tree" ;
